      "title": "Initializing Physical Volumes with LVM",
      "lectureOrder": 273,
      "videoOrder": 241,
      "sourceHash": "d57ae11643879a711abe2c88d29019ccf6ed84e714635d3e1a617d9715ecdc69",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.44,
          "end": 4.49,
          "en": "Let's now have a look at how we can initialize the physical volumes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.61,
          "end": 7.97,
          "en": "So we now want to recreate the setup from the lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.97,
          "end": 15.63,
          "en": "Before that, we have three hard drives and they all contribute to our llVM in with their storage space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 15.65,
          "end": 19.44,
          "en": "So the first step is that we need to initialize those volumes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 19.46,
          "end": 25.64,
          "en": "For this we have two options, but actually we only have one and that's that we need to initialize a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 25.64,
          "end": 27.91,
          "en": "part of the disk for llVM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 27.92,
          "end": 31.97,
          "en": "We will also have a look at the other option, but that one we should not do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 31.97,
          "end": 36.47,
          "en": "But so the way to go is that we initialize a part of the disk.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 36.47,
          "end": 40.19,
          "en": "So we would launch, for example, part for our disk.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 40.58,
          "end": 46.82,
          "en": "Be aware we might need to put a sudo in front of that for that disk and then we create a new partition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 46.82,
          "end": 48.74,
          "en": "there with the part command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 49.01,
          "end": 51.05,
          "en": "We say it should be a primary partition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 51.05,
          "end": 54.95,
          "en": "That should start at the beginning of our disk until the end of our disk.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.95,
          "end": 63.09,
          "en": "So yes, we only initialize llVM for a part of our disk or for one partition on our disk, but at the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 63.09,
          "end": 66.63,
          "en": "end this partition is the full our full disk pretty much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 67.23,
          "end": 71.7,
          "en": "So we create a partition and then we allocate that one to llVM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 71.7,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "So we create this partition with MK part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 75.03,
          "end": 78.42,
          "en": "Then we need to set the type of that partition to llVM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 78.42,
          "end": 83.03999999999999,
          "en": "So we say set then the number of that partition that should usually be the number one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 83.07,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "Then we say llvm on, that's a flag that we set there to indicate that this partition is used by llVM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 90.72,
          "end": 96.84,
          "en": "then we can exit part it and then we can run PV, create on that partition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 97.86,
          "en": "PV create.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 97.86,
          "end": 98.55,
          "en": "Why that one?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 98.55,
          "end": 104.82,
          "en": "Well, it's a physical volume, that's why it's with PV and we want to create a physical volume on this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 104.82,
          "end": 105.66,
          "en": "partition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 105.66,
          "end": 109.35,
          "en": "Let's have a look at this so I can start part it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 109.35,
          "end": 112.74000000000001,
          "en": "And the easiest way is if I just started on dev SDB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 112.77000000000001,
          "end": 115.02000000000001,
          "en": "This is my second hard disk.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 115.2,
          "end": 120.87,
          "en": "Please be aware if you run this on your computer, it depends on the order of those disks, but usually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 120.87,
          "end": 122.07,
          "en": "that should be the second drive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 122.1,
          "end": 124.89,
          "en": "That's and it should rather be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 124.89,
          "end": 126.63,
          "en": "Usually it should be constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 127.14,
          "end": 131.73,
          "en": "Like one drive should not be sometimes the second drive and then the third and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 137.64,
          "en": "So if we see it here, we can see here this is an unrecognized disk label in the sense that for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 137.64,
          "end": 139.92000000000002,
          "en": "we don't even have a partition table here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 140.13,
          "end": 142.95,
          "en": "Let's now try to create a partition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 143.31,
          "end": 145.5,
          "en": "MK Part primary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 146.54,
          "end": 148.57999999999998,
          "en": "Uh, from 0 to 100%.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 148.57999999999998,
          "end": 152.74,
          "en": "And then we can see here we do get this error message, unrecognized disk label.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 152.75,
          "end": 157.34,
          "en": "This is because we first have to initialize that disk with a partition table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 157.52,
          "end": 160.09,
          "en": "So what I need to do this clear work here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 160.1,
          "end": 161.02,
          "en": "Nope, it doesn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 161.03,
          "end": 162.89,
          "en": "But at least we get the help here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 163.28,
          "end": 170.54,
          "en": "We need to create a partition table now and we can do this by creating a disk label.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 170.57,
          "end": 171.29,
          "en": "MK Label.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 171.29,
          "end": 172.85,
          "en": "That's the partition table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 173.57,
          "end": 178.37,
          "en": "So I can say MK label to create a disk label or partition table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 179.13,
          "end": 182.96,
          "en": "So I can say here MK label to create that partition table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 182.97,
          "end": 189.54,
          "en": "I say the disk label type should be GPT and now it will warn me that there's an existing disk label.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 189.54,
          "end": 194.94,
          "en": "If this is the first initialization initialization of that disk, it should not warn you like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 194.94,
          "end": 200.49,
          "en": "I had to rerecord this because I felt like everything I was doing was too much at the bottom of the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 200.49,
          "end": 200.91,
          "en": "screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "So I'm now overwriting that partition table that I had created the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 208.38,
          "end": 214.56,
          "en": "But here we have now created that partition table and now we can see here we now have a partition table",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 214.56,
          "end": 216.99,
          "en": "and right now there are no partitions there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 216.99,
          "end": 218.94,
          "en": "Now I want to create a partition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 218.94,
          "end": 224.94,
          "en": "I want to create a primary partition from that starts at the beginning and goes until the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 224.94,
          "end": 230.7,
          "en": "So I say MK part we can see here the resulting partition is not properly aligned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 230.7,
          "end": 233.82,
          "en": "So what I can do is that I can just cancel that one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 233.82,
          "end": 234.92000000000002,
          "en": "Let's see what happened.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 234.93,
          "end": 235.86,
          "en": "Nothing has happened.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 235.86,
          "end": 237.32999999999998,
          "en": "We need to align it now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 241.24,
          "en": "I think if I say 0% then it should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 241.24,
          "end": 247.57,
          "en": "And then we can see here we have now created this partition and it's now aligned to those physical sectors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 247.57,
          "end": 250.39,
          "en": "So that can give us a little bit of performance improvement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 250.9,
          "end": 257.29,
          "en": "Um, we can see here now that we now have a partition with the number one and now we want to initialize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 257.29,
          "end": 258.01,
          "en": "this one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 258.04,
          "end": 263.35,
          "en": "Um, no, before we can initialize that one for llVM, we need to set the llVM flag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 263.35,
          "end": 267.01,
          "en": "So I say set one llvm on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 267.19,
          "end": 275.65,
          "en": "Now we can see here, if I say print that here there's this flag llVM and this just tells other programs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 275.65,
          "end": 277.96,
          "en": "that this partition is used by llVM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 277.96,
          "end": 281.11,
          "en": "So I can now quit it and I'm done here now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 281.2,
          "end": 289.25,
          "en": "So now my disk, if we have a look at this in Gparted, for example, we can see here in this gooey",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 290.17,
          "end": 298.81,
          "en": "SDB that we got this partition here, 50 gig GB bytes and we can see here there's no data on it, but",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 298.81,
          "end": 299.71,
          "en": "there's this flag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 299.71,
          "end": 303.58,
          "en": "llVM So this is pretty much what we did with part so far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 303.82,
          "end": 309.76,
          "en": "The next thing we can do is that we can allocate that space for as a physical volume.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 310.35,
          "end": 315.09,
          "en": "So what I can do here is that I say PV create slash dev sdb1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 315.09,
          "end": 324.96,
          "en": "I should select this partition here and I should also be extra careful not to accidentally do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 324.96,
          "end": 326.55,
          "en": "like this and then hit enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 326.55,
          "end": 328.11,
          "en": "So I should be rather careful here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 328.11,
          "end": 334.29,
          "en": "There are some checks here, so it might happen that it will then want us to confirm what we are doing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 334.29,
          "end": 335.82,
          "en": "But still this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 335.82,
          "end": 337.62,
          "en": "This can be rather risky.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 337.62,
          "end": 342.09000000000003,
          "en": "So I do this one here and now we can see here it has detected this is a partition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 342.09000000000003,
          "end": 343.53,
          "en": "There is nothing on that one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 344.37,
          "end": 348.87,
          "en": "And this physical volume has now successfully been created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 348.87,
          "end": 354.63,
          "en": "If we now have a look at Gparted, how it's going to visualize that one we can see here in terms of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 354.63,
          "end": 360.18,
          "en": "Gparted, it has just detected that there is a file system on it for Lvm2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 360.89,
          "end": 363.41,
          "en": "So we can see here it's detecting that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 364.04,
          "end": 368.66,
          "en": "So now we got our first physical volume that we created successfully.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 369.63,
          "end": 375.35,
          "en": "Um, I told you before that we have two options, but that we actually only have one because we could",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 375.35,
          "end": 381.47,
          "en": "also initialize or run the PV, create on the whole disk and not on that just one partition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 381.68,
          "end": 383.63,
          "en": "But this can cause a few problems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 383.63,
          "end": 390.86,
          "en": "The first one is that once we have a partition table, especially if we have a partition table, that's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 390.86,
          "end": 392.18,
          "en": "the more modern format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 392.78,
          "end": 396.40999999999997,
          "en": "Um, then it will refuse to overwrite that partition table at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 396.40999999999997,
          "end": 401.87,
          "en": "Even if we try to use additional parameters like minus F to force it to overwrite, it's not going to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 401.87,
          "end": 402.74,
          "en": "do that one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 403.31,
          "end": 405.53,
          "en": "So it's not going to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 405.53,
          "end": 411.92,
          "en": "In that case, if we already have a partition table there in the form of geo ID, And we also should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 411.92,
          "end": 419.33,
          "en": "avoid this because a lot of other programs, um, well, they would just see this as a disk then and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 419.33,
          "end": 428.1,
          "en": "right now the way they see it is if we look at Gparted again, that yes, SDB is now a disk, but it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 428.1,
          "end": 429.27,
          "en": "has a partition table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 429.27,
          "end": 435.45,
          "en": "And this partition table tells, for example, Gparted, that this area is now being used by Lvm2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 435.75,
          "end": 441.06,
          "en": "So this is the way to go, that we create a partition table also so that other programs, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 441.06,
          "end": 445.89,
          "en": "gparted know what's going on here and that maybe we shouldn't touch it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 445.89,
          "end": 455.73,
          "en": "So this is why I would recommend you not to, um, to run PV, create directly on your device, but",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 455.73,
          "end": 457.23,
          "en": "only on your partition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 457.74,
          "end": 461.82,
          "en": "And then it's better to let the partition span 100% of the device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 462.24,
          "end": 467.19,
          "en": "Once we have initialized the volume, we can list our physical volumes with PVS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 467.28,
          "end": 470.01,
          "en": "That's like the short form or PV display.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 470.04,
          "end": 473.13,
          "en": "That's like a more long form if we want more output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 473.13,
          "end": 474.65999999999997,
          "en": "So let's just have a look here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 474.65999999999997,
          "end": 483.93,
          "en": "So here we can see here PVS, we can see here we got Dev Sdb1 right now as a physical volume and we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 483.93,
          "end": 493.77,
          "en": "can see here 50GB and uh, 50GB free lvm2 And we can also say PV display, and then we can see we see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 493.77,
          "end": 494.82,
          "en": "a little bit more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 495.09,
          "end": 498.12,
          "en": "We can also see quite a few other information here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 498.12,
          "end": 500.79,
          "en": "Physical for the physical extent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 500.79,
          "end": 506.73,
          "en": "That's like a it equals like a block on like a hard disk level that we don't work with bytes, but like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 506.73,
          "end": 507.72,
          "en": "with groups of those.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 507.72,
          "end": 509.31,
          "en": "And what's the size there?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 509.88,
          "end": 510.99,
          "en": "It's here zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
